Package: odispers
Type: Package
Title: River-Network Dispersal Models for Onchocerciasis Prevalence
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Emanuele", "Giorgi", email = "e.giorgi@bham.ac.uk",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits exposure models for disease prevalence in which vector
    breeding takes place on a river network, exposure at each location
    accumulates from all river segments within a dispersal range, and the
    dispersal range depends on aridity. Exposure is computed by quadrature
    over the network with a compactly supported Wendland kernel, so that
    prevalence is exactly zero beyond the reach of any river. This version
    implements the model without latent random fields, fitted by maximum
    likelihood, and with a Whittle-Matern field on the river network in the
    breeding intensity, fitted by a Laplace approximation.
